# Haus Of Estate standalone Sanity Studio

This folder is a separate React/Vite application alongside `Haus-of-Estate`.
It connects to the existing Sanity project `jdxbkry4`, dataset `production`.
Schemas and editorial actions are imported from the Release 2 app source, so
Florence property fields and editorial approvals have one source of truth.

```powershell
cd C:/Users/surya/OneDrive/Documents/ChatGPT/studio-haus-of-estate
npm.cmd install
npm.cmd run dev
```

Open http://localhost:3333 and sign in with the account Deb invited to Sanity.
The CLI can be authenticated separately with `npx.cmd sanity login`.
The local initializer could not authenticate automatically on this machine.

Run `npm.cmd run schema:validate`, `npm.cmd run typecheck`, and `npm.cmd run build`
to verify local configuration. These do not publish documents or deploy the Studio.
The production dataset is an explicit choice from the supplied setup instructions.

The Next.js app runs separately on http://localhost:3000. Set
`SANITY_STUDIO_PREVIEW_ORIGIN` in an untracked `.env.local` to change its preview
origin. Draft preview also requires the app's server-only Sanity read token and
matching Sanity CORS configuration. Never put secret tokens in `SANITY_STUDIO_*`.
Use `localhost`, not `127.0.0.1`: the existing project accepts the localhost
Studio origin, while the IP address displays Sanity's CORS connection prompt.

`npm.cmd run typegen` extracts the shared schema and scans frontend queries. Its
generated output stays in this folder until the app adopts query result types.
Content import, publication, cloud schema deployment, and Studio deployment are
separate actions; this local setup performs none of them.
